      <li>
        <strong>Strict Filing Window:</strong> Appeals must be filed with the county Board of Equalization (BOE) by July 1st or within 60 days of receiving your official Value Change Notice (whichever is later).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Burden of Proof:</strong> The assessor's valuation is presumed correct by law. You must present clear, cogent, and convincing evidence (such as market sales comps) showing the assessed value exceeds true fair market value.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Focus on Comparable Sales:</strong> Your strongest evidence consists of 3 to 5 arm's-length sales of similar homes in your immediate neighborhood that occurred prior to January 1st of the assessment year.
      </li>
